/-!
# Hilbert geometry of scores

This file develops the Hilbert-space framework of semiparametric statistics on `L²(P) = Lp ℝ 2 P`:
mean-zero square-integrable functions, tangent spaces, efficient scores and efficient information
matrices, the conditional expectation score operator, and the projection formula onto the range of
a score operator. This geometry underlies pathwise differentiability, canonical gradients
(efficient influence functions), and semiparametric information bounds.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.meanZeroL2`: the closed subspace `L²₀(P)` of mean-zero elements of `L²(P)`, defined as
  the orthogonal complement of the constants.
* `TauCeti.tangentSpace`: the closed linear span of a set of scores in `L²(P)`.
* `TauCeti.efficientScore`: the residual `ℓ - Π_N ℓ` of a score `ℓ` after orthogonal projection
  onto the nuisance tangent space generated by `N`.
* `TauCeti.informationMatrix`: the Gram matrix `Iᵢⱼ = ⟪ℓᵢ, ℓⱼ⟫` of an indexed family of scores.
* `TauCeti.efficientInformationMatrix`: the Gram matrix of the efficient scores
  `i ↦ efficientScore P N (ℓ i)`.
* `TauCeti.pullbackL2`: composition `g ↦ g ∘ m` along a measurable map `m`, as an isometry
  `L²(η.map m) → L²(η)`.
* `TauCeti.condExpOperator`: the Hilbert-space adjoint `L²(η) → L²(η.map m)` of `pullbackL2`,
  representing conditional expectation given `m` on the image space.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.mem_meanZeroL2_iff`, `TauCeti.isCompl_span_const_meanZeroL2`,
  `TauCeti.starProjection_meanZeroL2_apply`, `TauCeti.starProjection_meanZeroL2_eq_sub_const`,
  `TauCeti.norm_sq_starProjection_meanZeroL2`: the orthogonal splitting `L²(P) = span {1} ⊕ L²₀(P)`,
  the centering projection, and its squared norm as the variance.
* `TauCeti.meanZeroL2_subset_closure_bounded`,
  `TauCeti.meanZeroL2_subset_closure_boundedContinuous`: density of bounded (and bounded
  continuous) mean-zero functions in `L²₀(P)`.
* `TauCeti.tangentSpace_union`, `TauCeti.toSubmodule_tangentSpace_union_of_isOrtho`,
  `TauCeti.starProjection_tangentSpace_union_of_isOrtho`: union of tangent sets and additivity of
  orthogonal projections onto orthogonal tangent spaces.
* `TauCeti.posSemidef_informationMatrix_sub_efficientInformationMatrix`,
  `TauCeti.efficientInformationMatrix_eq_informationMatrix_iff`,
  `TauCeti.posSemidef_efficientInformationMatrix_sub_of_subset`,
  `TauCeti.posDef_efficientInformationMatrix_iff`: the information-loss inequalities, the
  orthogonality criterion for adaptation, and the linear-independence criterion for positive
  definiteness.
* `TauCeti.pullbackL2_condExpOperator_ae_eq`, `TauCeti.condExpOperator_comp_pullbackL2`,
  `TauCeti.condExpOperator_surjective`, `TauCeti.norm_condExpOperator_le_one`,
  `TauCeti.map_meanZeroL2_condExpOperator`: characterization of `condExpOperator` as conditional
  expectation given `m`, contraction and surjectivity, and surjectivity onto `L²₀(η.map m)`.
* `TauCeti.starProjection_tangentSpace_range_eq`: the projection formula `A (A† A)⁻¹ A†` for a
  score operator `A` with invertible information operator `A† A`.

## References

* A. W. van der Vaart, *Asymptotic Statistics*, Cambridge University Press, 1998, §25.2, §25.4,
  §25.5.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

